        "id": "511096",
        "date_added": "2026-10-19 16:33:59",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "protokol-client: undocumented Linux bot (not a Mirai fork); x86-64 build captured on a Telnet honeypot (s7cn4.x86 via hxxp://184.174.96.216/ and ftp :2121). All 328 strings ChaCha20-encrypted in one table (0x41f8c0, key 0x4212a0, nonce 0x421280), hence low AV detection. C2 list reached three ways: hardcoded slot (empty in this build, default port 7443); DNS TXT dead drops imaweirdo[.]my, paranoidjuice[.]info, smithsonn-s[.]top, howtodisappearcompletely[.]zip queried directly at public resolvers (hex + ChaCha20, key 64a86390d6b2df656cf515c92340f1bc435295d37671b8466e4dc096dc38ee70, nonce 506674fc5875ec3f2a5307c0); BitTorrent DHT BEP44 get on target ff346dce37389086fa8d9e040eff35a4505e9a35 (same key), second list on target 9808eee4afb97ccf6e9bf703ecd90972cabe2b35. C2 handshake: Noise-NK-style X25519 with pinned server key 314bc91bd4e8b6c5b05bd4453017581592dfeb79ea512f7d09c0416034881117 (labels protokol-v1-nk / -conf / -resume / -bc-nk). Capabilities: game/HTTP/TLS DDoS, XMRig control, SOCKS4/5 + back-connect proxy, self-update with hash check, LAN recon, competitor killer (Mirai drops, frpc/chisel/ligolo/rsocks), iptables port open; renames itself 'crond'. Windows build implied (protokol-client.exe, Run key 'protokol service'). Static (Ghidra) + sandboxed run."
      }
    ],
